A brutally unforgiving platformer whose sheer level of difficulty harkens back to the blister-busting days of the NES.  Hard as hell, yes - but the design is excellent, the theme is delightfully tacky and the controls are super-tight.
All in all, Super Meat Boy is a "white-knuckle, grit your teeth with frustration then end up cheering with elation" kind of game.  This one gives you the thrill of beating sadistically, yet skillfully designed levels again and again.
I keep coming back to this one.  Hope you're ready for a challenge.     ^ ^;

